{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nusage-log rows (src/rebar/llm/usage_log.py) record the four token fields but not model, provider, or timestamp, and the plan-review budget shedder prices work with hard-coded guesses (COST_SINGLE_TURN_USD=0.006, COST_AGENT_USD=0.12, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py:107-109). No provider publishes a machine-readable price API; pydantic's genai-prices package bundles offline price data with cache read/write tiers, historical prices by timestamp, and a typed LookupError for unknown models. Operator approved it as an optional add-in with graceful fallback.\n\n## Approach\n(1) Extend usage_log.record to record(usage, *, op, model=None, provider=None) plus a UTC ISO timestamp written inside record(); update its single call site at runner.py:547 to pass model=ran_model and the provider inferred by the existing mapping at src/rebar/llm/config.py:321-327. (2) summarize reads plain JSONL dicts (not live usage objects), so pricing maps row fields explicitly: build genai_prices' usage input from the stored dict — input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_read_tokens, cache_write_tokens keyword-mapped one-to-one — and call calc_price with the row's model, provider, and parsed timestamp. No reliance on pydantic-ai objects at summarize time; the mapping is a pure dict-to-kwargs adapter function with its own unit test. (3) summarize keeps its existing grouping by op and adds cost: per-row cost from that row's own model/provider/timestamp (a multi-model op sums correctly row by row); the report prints per-op est. cost plus a per-model rollup table. (4) Pricing is attempted only when `import genai_prices` succeeds; each calc_price call is wrapped in `except Exception` (pricing must never break summarize): LookupError marks the row unpriced, any other exception logs at WARNING and marks the row unpriced; the summary reports \"excludes N unpriced calls\". When the package is absent, summarize prints token totals with the cost column reading \"unavailable (install rebar[pricing])\". (5) New optional extra `pricing = [\"genai-prices\"]` in pyproject.toml. Never a hard error, never a silently-wrong number; the column is labeled \"est. cost\". Alternative rejected: vendoring LiteLLM's ~2 MB price JSON — takes on key-normalization and schema-drift ownership that genai-prices maintains upstream.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/usage_log.py, src/rebar/llm/runner.py (record call site), pyproject.toml, tests/unit/test_usage_log.py (extend), docs/llm-framework.md (usage-log section).\n\n## Testing\nUnit: rows gain the three new fields via the updated record signature; the dict-to-kwargs adapter maps all four token fields and tolerates missing keys (defaults 0); summarize with a stubbed genai_prices prices known rows, marks unknown-model rows unpriced via LookupError, marks a malformed-row pricing crash unpriced via the broad handler with a WARNING log, and totals annotate the exclusion; summarize with the import failing prints the unavailable message and exits 0; old-format rows without the new fields still summarize.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] New usage-log rows carry model, provider, and UTC timestamp, populated from the runner call site (checked: `pytest tests/unit/test_usage_log.py`).\n- [ ] The dict-to-kwargs adapter converts a stored row into genai-prices usage input covering all four token fields, defaulting absent fields to 0 (checked: adapter unit test).\n- [ ] With genai-prices importable, summarize prints per-op est. cost and a per-model rollup, marking unknown or crash rows unpriced without raising (checked: unit tests with a stubbed price module covering LookupError and a generic exception).\n- [ ] Without genai-prices, summarize prints token totals and \"unavailable (install rebar[pricing])\" and exits 0 (checked: unit test with import blocked).\n- [ ] Rows written by the previous format still summarize without error (checked: fixture test)."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785390726831838001,"uuid":"d446e706-54c2-4819-a791-f161b9657a48"}